# Never normalize line endings anywhere under the content tree.
#
# The binary formats (.png, .dds, .bsp, .ogg) carry NUL bytes early and git detects
# them correctly, but this tree also holds real text: .shader, .cfg, .skin, .mapinfo,
# .map. Those would get CRLF on a Windows checkout and LF on Linux, which makes
# tools/package.sh produce byte-different release zips from the same commit and makes
# the launcher's content-addressed asset-pack identity wobble.
#
# This lives inside the tree rather than as a root-level `data/** -text` pattern so it
# travels with the directory and cannot be defeated by pattern-precedence surprises.
# See planning/repo-restructure-2026-07-29.md gotcha G2.
* -text
